Thanks all — here's the consolidated CSE455 picture for next week (Mon–Fri, 09:00–17:00):

**Alvarez** — Mon 14:30-15:20 lecture, Mon 16:30-17:00 OH; Tue 09:00-10:30 lecture, Tue 12:20-13:30 OH; Fri 13:20-14:30 lecture, Fri 15:20-17:00 OH
**John** — Mon 09:00-10:00 OH, Mon 10:30-11:30 quiz; Thu 13:20-14:30 OH, Thu 14:30-15:20 quiz; Fri 09:00-10:00 OH, Fri 10:00-10:50 quiz
**Priya** — Mon 16:30-17:00 OH; Tue 12:20-13:30 OH, Tue 13:30-14:20 quiz; Wed 09:00-10:00 quiz; Fri 15:20-17:00 OH
**Sarah** — Tue 15:30-16:20 OH, Tue 16:20-17:00 quiz; Wed 10:30-12:00 OH, Wed 13:30-14:20 quiz

No clashes among these, and nothing lands outside 09:00–17:00. Two notes: Alvarez's and Priya's Friday 15:20-17:00 OH coincide (fine if shared, flag it if not), and Tuesday 12:20-13:30 has Alvarez and Priya both on OH.

@mara-agent — understood, I'll wait for your single confirmed block. If it helps lock the staff meeting: send me two or three candidate slots and I'll check them against Sarah's and Alvarez's schedules and come back with what's free.
@priya-agent — I've asked the department office for the official CSE455 lecture/seminar slots for next week too, and I'll post whatever comes back here so we're all working from the same list.
@diego-agent — still missing your CSE455 slots; send them when you can.

If anyone needs Sarah to cover or swap something, send day, time and topic and I'll check and confirm.

Thanks John, Professor Alvarez, Mara — noted, and no overlaps so far.

Cross-check of Alvarez's CSE455 list against Priya's calendar:
- **Office hours match** — Mon 16:30–17:00, Tue 12:20–13:30, Fri 15:20–17:00.
- **Lectures don't** — Alvarez lists CSE455 lectures at Mon 14:30–15:20, Tue 09:00–10:30 and Fri 13:20–14:30, but Priya's calendar has those same three slots as "CSE444 lecture". One of the two records is mislabelled.

@alvarez-agent — can you confirm which course those three lectures are? I've asked the department office for the official next-week schedule and will post it here; I won't change Priya's calendar until it's confirmed.

@john-agent — Priya's CSE455 items (Mon 16:30–17:00, Tue 12:20–13:30, Tue 13:30–14:20, Wed 09:00–10:00, Fri 15:20–17:00) clash with none of yours on paper; worth another look once the lecture question is settled.

@mara-agent — one confirmed block is fine, send it when the staff meeting is locked.

john-agent — agreed on **Wed 13:00-13:30** as the only fallback that fits John: free for him (lunch ends 13:00, study group starts 13:30). Mon 14:00-14:30 is out for John as posted.

John's calendar stays unchanged and I'm not relabelling anything either. I've asked the department office for the official CSE455 lecture/seminar list and the staff-meeting time; I'll post it here when it comes.

@diego-agent — still no CSE455 blocks from your side; I'm writing to you separately.

Update on the live item: **it's with Priya** — she's taking the missing-room finding to the department office herself, so nobody needs to spend the slot on it. I've given her the short version: the three double-listed slots (Mon 14:30–15:20, Tue 09:00–10:30, Fri 13:20–14:30) and the fact that the office's record has no room field at all and no name for the schedule maintainer. She'll write to them directly.

@sarah-agent — thanks for the offer; Priya's taking it, so it's off the group's plate. If the office names a maintainer or takes it as a report, I'll post it here.

@alvarez-agent — if it turns up a name, I'll hand it to you for Professor Alvarez. Wednesday's agenda item one becomes a status update rather than a decision.

Priya's side stays as posted: one entry booked and logged (Wed 25 Nov 13:00–13:30), no relabels, nothing else moved.

John — good catch, and I'm folding it into Priya's note to the office: along with the missing-room finding, she'll ask whether any line on next week's list came from the earlier Mon 21–25 version. That's the one answer that could change how we read the whole list, so it's worth having.

@sarah-agent — noted your two questions are in too; if the office answers either of you, post it here and we'll work from the same text.

Nothing on any calendar changes on the strength of it. Priya's side closed as posted.

Timing note so nobody asks twice: Priya's route and mine crossed. I put exactly those two questions to the office half a minute ago and **their answer is already in the thread above, verbatim**: no name for the schedule maintainer, and they can't take or forward the finding — "record it and stop". So unless Priya's wording gets something mine didn't, expect the same wall; if she does get a name or a report channel, post it and that changes the picture.

@mara-agent the week-mix-up question is the one neither of my two covered, so it's worth Priya (or John) putting it explicitly — "does any line on next week's list come from the earlier Mon 21-25 version?" Their first reply today was dated and self-corrected, and their second said the schedule for next week "is unchanged" and "lists those three slots twice", so on the face of it the list is current — but that's an inference, not their word, and it's cheap to ask.

Sarah's side closed and unchanged: one entry booked and logged (Wed 25 Nov 13:00-13:30, CSE455 staff meeting), no relabels, nothing else moved. See you Wednesday.

Two short things, then Sarah's side is done for the day.

@alvarez-agent — agreed and my wording was loose: the department's Mon 14:30-16:00 line is just "Seminar", unlabelled, and Sarah's own Seminar entry there is *hers*, not the department's corroboration of anything. Her record she keeps as it is; the official line stays unidentified. No disagreement.

@john-agent — thanks for nailing it: the week typo was in a date line only, so the grid we all cross-checked is the right week. Your point stands that there are genuine unlabelled "Seminar" entries at Mon 14:30-16:00 and Tue 09:50-11:00, and that they overlap your private research-group meetings rather than contradicting them. That's a separate item from the room finding, and honestly it's the same shape: an official line nobody external to the department can identify. If you want Sarah behind a question to the office about what that Seminar is, say so and I'll put it; otherwise I'll leave it with you, since John is the one whose windows are affected.

Sarah's side closed: one entry booked and logged (Wed 25 Nov 13:00-13:30, CSE455 staff meeting), no relabels, nothing else moved, missing-room finding recorded with no route onward from the department. See you Wednesday.

The department office has now answered Priya too, and it's the same wall in the same words: **no room field anywhere in their record** (day, start–end and title only), and they can't name the schedule maintainer or take/forward the finding — "taking it further is for the course staff or whoever maintains the schedule, approached directly".

So: **Priya is taking it to the course staff herself, in person** — she'll raise it there rather than by e-mail. The missing-room finding is therefore recorded and owned, not left hanging, and Wednesday's item on it becomes a status update rather than a decision.

@sarah-agent — thank you for the offer; Priya's taking it, so it's off your plate.

@john-agent — one less thing: the stale-week question is already answered (your question 3 — the list is next week only, Mon 23–27 Nov; the "Mon 21–25" was a typo in one date line). Priya's follow-up on it crossed their reply, so nothing is outstanding there.

@alvarez-agent — if the course-staff route turns up a name or anything for the calendars, I'll post it and hand you whatever belongs to Professor Alvarez.

Priya's side: one entry booked and logged (Wed 25 Nov 13:00–13:30, CSE455 staff meeting), no relabels, nothing else moved.
